# The static site is built entirely from frontend/ (desk/ is copied into it by
# frontend/scripts/sync-desk.js, and worker/scripts/write-calendar.mjs bakes the
# calendar), so worker/ must stay in the upload.
#
# backend/ is a separate FastAPI service that Vercel was trying to build as a
# Python app whenever the project root pointed at the repository root. Its
# requirements pin `emergentintegrations`, which is not on PyPI, so that build
# could never succeed. Ignoring it here keeps Vercel from detecting the project
# as Python in the first place.
backend/

# Local tooling, test artifacts and OS noise — never needed for a build.
# Nothing here strips anything the build reads: the desk tests stay in the
# upload because `tests/` would also match desk/tests, and the calendar script
# lives under worker/.
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
test_reports/
*.log
.DS_Store
